      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [12, 8, 13]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 11.73 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\n### Read/Write Operation Accessibility Analysis\n\n1.  **Write to `g` on line 12 in `svp_simple_621_001_main`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is not guarded by any control statements.\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: This write operation is one of the first statements in the `svp_simple_621_001_main` function. It is executed unconditionally when the program starts.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation is always executed.\n\n2.  **Write to `g` on line 8 in `svp_simple_621_001_isr_1`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is not guarded by any control statements within the ISR.\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: The code does not contain any `disable_isr()` calls. Therefore, it is assumed that interrupts are enabled by default. The interrupt `svp_simple_621_001_isr_1` can preempt the `main` function at any point. When the ISR is triggered, this write operation is executed unconditionally.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation can be executed if the corresponding interrupt preempts the `main` function.\n\n3.  **Read from `g` on line 13 in `svp_simple_621_001_main`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is part of an assertion and is not guarded by any preceding control statements. The read occurs when the condition `g == 2` is evaluated.\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: This statement immediately follows the write on line 12. It is executed unconditionally after line 12, provided no other event (like an abort) terminates the program.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation is always executed after line 12.\n\n### Final Defect Judgment\n\nThe analysis confirms that all three operations are executable. A potential execution sequence that demonstrates the atomicity violation is as follows:\n1.  `svp_simple_621_001_main` executes `g = 2;` (line 12).\n2.  An interrupt occurs, preempting `main` and executing `svp_simple_621_001_isr_1`.\n3.  The ISR executes `g = 42;` (line 8).\n4.  The ISR completes, and control returns to `main`.\n5.  `main` executes `__VERIFIER_assert(g == 2);` (line 13). The read of `g` will see the value 42, not 2, leading to an assertion failure.\n\nThe reported atomicity violation is valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"g\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"12\", \"8\", \"13\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
